note: Step 1: load an official library (DLC) and a custom module (module statements must stay on one line)
use DLC:network
use stage_data from ./maps/core_engine

note:
This is a multi-line comment area.
This code combines 1-based indexes, or_else, pattern matching, global and local variables, and more, as a final end-to-end check.
endnote

note: Step 2: core variables and constants (a constant is declared only with to)
set constant number MAX_LEVEL to 99
set constant str ENGINE_SIGNATURE to "CUFF_LANG_V1"

set number current_lvl to 1
set str user_email to "Player_One@CuffLang.com"
set list reward_tier_list to ["Gold", "Silver", "Bronze"]

note: Step 3: a returnable function that handles validation and text pattern matching
set returnable func audit_and_assess_user(email, lvl) do:
    note: to use a global value inside a function, connect it with global first
    change MAX_LEVEL to global

    note: check the email structure with pattern matching (using the is operator)
    if email is "[str]+@[str]2~10" do:
        print("Pattern matching: email structure verified")
    end

    note: combining the ! negation operator with a case-sensitive is comparison
    if !lvl is MAX_LEVEL do:
        print(f"Current level {lvl} is not the maximum level.")
    end

    if lvl is MAX_LEVEL do:
        return "epic_rank"
    else if lvl >= 50 do:
        return "rare_rank"
    else do:
        return "common_rank"
    end
end

note: Step 4: a standalone function that stands in for asynchronous data handling
set async func backup_user_cloud_data() do:
    print("Syncing a snapshot of the virtual machine's data to remote cloud infrastructure.")
end

note: Step 5: run the main logic and exercise 1-based collection handling
set str evaluation_result to audit_and_assess_user(user_email, current_lvl)

note: calling a function with an or_else safety net
await backup_user_cloud_data() or_else do:
    print("Working around a cloud sync failure caused by the network environment.")
end

note: with 1-based indexing, index 1 is the first element, "Gold".
print(f"Top-tier reward emblem: {reward_tier_list[1]}")

note: modifying the list with the standalone statements add to and change
add "None_Tier" to reward_tier_list
change reward_tier_list[1] to "Platinum_Tier" note: replace the existing word at position 1 with platinum

note: Step 6: fast iteration using the tilde range (~) and the loop repeat structure
loop repeat step to 1 ~ 5 do:
    if step is 4 do:
        print("Stopping the loop early.")
        stop
    end
    print(f"CuffScript fast VM sync engine running... current loop step: {step}")
end
